  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday through next Friday)\nIssued at 1040 PM CDT Thu Sep 10 2026\n\nBy Sunday we'll be on the back side of the departing system \naloft. This should be a great weather day as drier air moves into \nthe area, but with a quick recovery of low-level ridging. Above-\nnormal temperatures are forecast Sunday and will persist into much\nof next week thanks to a slow-moving deep-layer ridge that will \npersist. Rain and storm chances are quite low and mainly limited \nto mid to late next week when we start to see a little moisture \nrecovery to foster diurnal convection.",
